{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985631-enhanced-magick","id":985631,"title":"Enhanced magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T13:29:03-07:00","id":985631,"title":"Enhanced magick","content":"Well... We all know about abilities enhancing magick and magick enhancing abilities. What about magick enhancing magick ? I'll make myself as clear as possible with two exemples :<br /> - You need Quintessence during a ritual. And for that, you use a Prime 3 Effect to draw Quintessence for a nearby source (hopefully a Node). Do you roll separately your Prime 3 spell and the spell being the object of your ritual ? Or do you make only one succession of rolls with all the Spheres involved and splitting the successes to get Quintessence and perform the ritual at the same time ?<br /> - May be more relevent now. You're using a gun to shoot at someone with bullet enhanced with Forces. Moreover, you use supportive spells, let's say an Entropy 1 &quot;Hit the weak spot&quot; Effect. Now, how do you count the Entropy 1 spell in regard of the Mage that only uses Forces.<br /> <br /> My question here is the following: do you find legit to roll supportive spell the same way you roll abilities before doing magick ? In the second exemple, each success on the Entropy 1 effect would lower the difficulty by one of the magick attack. Or do you only count the Forces Effect to count the damage (and get the automatic success), then count the successes of the Arete roll to lower the difficulty of the hit cause of the Entropy 1 effect ?<br /> <br /> The question is valid for any supportive spell you can cast. Another exemple for that : You want to destroy a thick amored metallic door. You can use a Forces Effect and use the busting things chart, and some Mages could add Matter 1 or Entropy 3 to make the task easier. What advantage do you give to those Mages ? After all, learning the true components of the door or degrading its material could either be a solution to make the action easier. Do you find legit to roll a Matter 1 Effect counting as a &quot;magick enhances magick&quot; roll ?<br /> <br /> Hope it's clear. Thank you for you answers !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:45:27-07:00","id":986898,"title":"","content":"you can only do one magic thing a round, so if you wanted to do the entropy forces thing, you would have to roll and split dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:30:19-07:00","id":986921,"title":"","content":"You can split Arete rolls ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T22:13:13-07:00","id":987097,"title":"","content":"Quintessence for ritual:<br /> One effect that builds up ober time<br /> <br /> Weak spot+Forces enhanced bullet<br /> If you want to do it in 1 turn I would say it is Magick enhances Abilities and you have to split your successes on extra damage and diff reduction (You could also do with 1 of the spheres alone)<br /> <br /> Two allied mages(or one mage with a Talisman) can divide the work between them:<br /> One finds a weak spot and fires his gun at it, the other enhances the bullet.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow magick enhancing magick as a mechanic, but it might lower the successes needed or the TN of your spell, if you point out how the sphere in question helps your intention.<br /> <br /> Splitting Arete on two effects is not in M20 anymore IRC.<br /> Just splitting Arete and a mundane action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:27:04-07:00","id":987302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985631-enhanced-magick?p=987097#post987097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quintessence for ritual:<br /> One effect that builds up ober time</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand it. Could you clarify please ? Do you mean you manage the Effect as a &quot;Damage Over Time&quot; Effect ? Meaning the Mage would perform a Prime 2/3 Effect and split the successes between gain (which would be the amount of Quintessence obtained per turn) and duration ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985631-enhanced-magick?p=987097#post987097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weak spot+Forces enhanced bullet<br /> If you want to do it in 1 turn I would say it is Magick enhances Abilities and you have to split your successes on extra damage and diff reduction (You could also do with 1 of the spheres alone)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow magick enhancing magick as a mechanic, but it might lower the successes needed or the TN of your spell, if you point out how the sphere in question helps your intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I do it for now but I'm only partially satisfied with that answer. I'm trying to find a midway solution between :<br /> - Doing it narratively meaning that the player has to point out how the Sphere helps him,<br /> - Doing it mechanically with two Effects.<br /> <br /> This is easiest with the rituals because it is not really part of an action. In combat, you do not have the time to cast two Effects that would be :<br /> - Entropy 1 to find the weak spots (and may be extend it to the whole fight),<br /> - Forces (of other kind of Effect) to actually shoot.<br /> <br /> Having a single action for all that makes sense I think. After all, the Effect is summarized as this: I want to shoot hard (Forces) him in his weak spot (Entropy). Simple enough to be doned in one round. Or I may be mistaken because nothing's simple... Dunno.<br /> <br /> May be the solution is just to prepare. After all... this is true for most Mages in most cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985631-enhanced-magick?p=987097#post987097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splitting Arete on two effects is not in M20 anymore IRC.<br /> Just splitting Arete and a mundane action.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it was possible before ? People often talk about Revised rules, but I only read Mage 2 and Mage 20 (I would wait for Mage 200 for my next update on the rules ^^).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:57:30-07:00","id":987459,"title":"","content":"Quintessence in a ritual adds Prime 3 as a requirement and it is stated that you gain double successes in quint. Be careful tough, more than 10 makes the effect vulgar IRC.<br /> Duration is also an option.<br /> <br /> As long as the magick doesn't reduce its own TN I would be convincabke to let it fly.<br /> Split your successes between the two effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:43:59-07:00","id":988739,"title":"","content":"Regarding the &quot;Hitting the Weak spot&quot; effect plus Forces enhanced bullet i'd rule it something like this;<br /> When you fire a gun as an ordinary action in this system you only fire, you don't aim. This means that you could have the effect take place in separate turns. First one for aiming+&quot;Hitting the Weak spot&quot; where the magick action enhances the regular action and the second one for shooting+enhanced bullet where the magickal effect enhances the shot.<br /> With training you could learn to do this as a Rote where both magical effects are combined into one effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:58:55-07:00","id":989032,"title":"","content":"I think I'll do it as I thought and as Nonsense suggested it for now. If the player points out why he uses a specific Sphere, I'll give him an advantage by reducing the difficulty.<br /> <br /> However, I'll do some tests and submit it to my players because I like the idea of spliting the successes in the different parts of the Effect. After all, successes are already split in Damage/Duration/Targets, why would I not add to Extra-Effect to that list ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:21:34-07:00","id":989232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985631-enhanced-magick?p=989032#post989032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll do it as I thought and as Nonsense suggested it for now. If the player points out why he uses a specific Sphere, I'll give him an advantage by reducing the difficulty.<br /> <br /> However, I'll do some tests and submit it to my players because I like the idea of spliting the successes in the different parts of the Effect. After all, successes are already split in Damage/Duration/Targets, why would I not add to Extra-Effect to that list ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only concern of mine is with pre-casted effects (mind-shield, stat boosting, etc.). When a enchantment to boost your physique also grants a mind-shield and an extra action you saved yourself the trouble of upkeeping two effects.<br /> <br /> Edit: Solution is so simple, each effect counts, no matter if you achieve 3 with one spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Found an answer myself 10-18-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}